+# End-to-end Python workflow study
+
+Produce a navigable map of the requested branch or checkout: actual entry points, control flow, data/artifact contracts, process boundaries, recovery behavior, and the Python modules that implement them. Keep documentation of current behavior separate from a requested audit or improvement task.
+
+## Establish what source is authoritative
+
+Read the current handoff, Git status, and recent history. Resolve the user's branch/worktree choice before following older architecture notes. A branch under active development may have a different engine, artifact schema, or recovery contract from main. Historical notes and existing maps are leads until checked against the selected source.
+
+Record the selected commit and any local edits that affect the study. When the user requests committed branch behavior, read dirty files through `git show <commit>:<path>` or a temporary source mirror; preserve the live checkout. When the user requests the working tree, include its changed bytes and label them. Do not silently switch between these two interpretations. Never copy credentials or saved private runs into a source mirror.
+
+An inventory should record each scoped Python path, line count, hash, owner, and review depth. Inventorying or parsing a file is not reading it. Separate application source, tests inspected as evidence, vendored runtime boundaries, generated code, and explicitly excluded material. Retain small scripts and package initializers when they participate in startup or import behavior.
+
+## Divide the study without losing the workflow
+
+Use delegated readers only when the user or applicable instructions authorize delegation. Assign disjoint areas and output files. Split very large modules by explicit line ranges; reconcile those ranges into one file-level result. Read in chunks small enough that tool output remains complete. If output is truncated, read the missing portion before claiming full coverage.
+
+Give each reader the same source authority and a concrete question. Useful areas include orchestration/state, research/tools, data/graph/identity, preparation/runtime, reports/publication, UI/API, and operations. The coordinator should trace cross-area boundaries while readers work, rather than independently repeating every area study.
+
+Require source anchors, caller/callee relationships, emitted/consumed artifacts, relevant schemas/hashes/identities, error and fallback paths, and explicit uncertainties. Readers should report actual read ranges and distinguish a direct read from inference. Existing diagrams and comments do not establish that a path is active; follow the caller.
+
+## Reconcile boundaries before synthesis
+
+Trace a representative user scenario from its public entry point to its final consumer. For each handoff, identify the producer, payload or persisted file, validation/admission rule, consumer, and stopping condition. Include restart/resume/fork/cancellation behavior when present. Check that an intermediate successful status is not being described as a published or usable deliverable.
+
+Look explicitly at subprocess interpreters, runtime overlays, MCP/HTTP boundaries, queues/IPC, and process-local registries versus durable state. Configuration names and source defaults can be documented without reading secret values. A copied runtime file may differ from its tracked producer; label whether runtime deployment was inspected or merely described from code.
+
+Review the synthesized boundary claims independently when the study is broad enough to justify it. Resolve conflicting descriptions in source. Validate coverage unions, source hashes, cited paths/line anchors, and document links. A coverage receipt supports the reported read scope; it does not prove that every interpretation is correct.
+
+## Deliver and stop
+
+Write one concise workflow spine with links to granular area reports and the module inventory. State the selected source, exclusions, static versus executed checks, unresolved facts, and a useful next-session starting point. Do not launch paid pipelines, mutate saved runs, import side-effectful application modules, or run integration tests merely to support a source-only familiarization task. If execution is requested, use the project's applicable verification procedure and report that evidence separately.
+
+The study is complete when its requested scope is accounted for, the public workflow and important alternative paths are connected, material boundary discrepancies are resolved or explicitly qualified, and the durable report can answer where and how the behavior occurs without repeating the original discovery work.
